# Shape lemmas for the canonical binary naturals, enabled with the type
# check beside hindley_milner_unions and prolog_backend_shapes, after
# prolog_backend_shapes' shapes of the naturals and the booleans: a structure
# of three alternatives, the first with no field and the other two with one
# field each, is a candidate for `binary_set true`, the filter whose members
# the family binary_natural holds at the parameter true (binary_prolog_backend,
# `native_specialization(binary_natural)` on binary_set), and so are its two
# fields. Every other lemma that writes typed versions and contracts is
# prolog_backend_shapes', one for every representation, so this module adds
# the shape of one representation only: a new representation adds attractors
# and repellers, never lemmas. The
# candidacy is positive, read from one layer, with no closed-world step: a
# value of the shape that is no canonical binary natural (a leading zero,
# binary_even binary_zero) is filtered out by `binary_set true` and its
# typed version's fallback takes the untyped path, as prolog_backend_shapes
# says of a candidate whose values are not the representation's.
#
# The schemes of four operations of the module binary, as
# native_arithmetic_unions writes double's: each takes two binary naturals and
# gives one, B below the recursive type of the three alternatives.
#
# Each lemma states its soundness claim above it, after the section of the
# paper proof its declaration cites. Used together with the natives of the four operations
# (binary_operations_wren_backend).

